      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nUse OpenSees to analyze a 22 m single-bay portal with a horizontal roof at z = 7 m and two fixed column bases. The roof has three piecewise constant sections: B1 over x = 0–5 m, B2 over x = 5–17 m, and B3 over x = 17–22 m. Apply a global downward 6 kN/m load to the entire roof in case D. The x = 11 m midpoint is a connected observation node splitting B2 into two identical segments. Report ux, uz and ry at x = 5, 11 and 17 m; N, V3 and M2 immediately on both sides of each section boundary at x = 5 and 17 m; and Fx, Fz and My at both column bases. Include a section-segmentation table showing each roof segment, x limits and assigned section. Use the piecewise constant properties and rigid joints in the public appendices.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
